// spec: MOD-008, MOD-013
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// MOD-008 accepts both imports below.  MOD-013 then refuses only the AMBIGUOUS
// BARE USE, and the qualifier resolves it.  So this program should print:
//
//     from Alpha        (Alpha.Shared, qualified)
//     from Beta         (Beta.Shared, qualified -- a different function)
//     only in Alpha     (bare, exported by only Alpha -- unambiguous)
//     only in Beta      (bare, exported by only Beta -- unambiguous)
//
// and only then be refused, at the bare 'Shared', with
// ''Shared' is ambiguous: Alpha or Beta.'
//
// The second IMPORT is refused instead, with ''Shared' is already defined;
// mark it private in one of the modules.' -- advice to edit a module because
// of what some other module happens to export.

uses 'modules/Alpha';
uses 'modules/Beta';

WriteLn (Alpha.Shared ());
WriteLn (Beta.Shared ());

WriteLn (OnlyAlpha ());
WriteLn (OnlyBeta ());

WriteLn (Shared ());
